  <prompt>
    RE-SCOPED 2026-07-09 (Path C, CLAUDE.md §6.5) — the original prompt named two RETRACTED "invented"
    PaneEventBus discriminants (`compose_action_request` / `compose_edit_apply_request`) that Spike 0 +
    design.md §7.2 + ComposeEditor.tsx JSDoc + useSerialActionQueue.ts explicitly forbid. The real,
    published contract is `compose-contracts.ts`. Wire the client dispatch path for the five R2 catalog
    actions using the SHIPPED flows, adding ZERO new PaneEventBus discriminants:
    (1) The dispatch TRIGGER is the DIRECT Click-path seam — `dispatchConsumer(bindingId, {slots})` →
        `POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{id}/dispatch` → `SessionDispatchOrchestrator` → `GetBindingByIdAsync`
        → prompted executor. Already wired: ComposeEditor mounts `ComposeAiToolbar` (task 030) with
        `enqueueComposeAction`; ConversationPane exposes `dispatchComposeAction` via `useSerialActionQueue`
        → `createConsumerDispatcher`. VERIFY/COMPLETE the offer→dispatch hand-off (ComposeWorkspace threading
        `ConversationPane.dispatchComposeAction` → `ComposeEditor.enqueueComposeAction`).
    (2) Flow 2 is the EXISTING `conversation.compose_selection_offer` (ComposeEditor already emits it via
        `useSelectionEventDispatch`) — pane choreography, not the trigger; confirm it is consumed.
    (3) The draft-alternative apply leg emits the EXISTING `workspace.compose_assistant_insert` discriminant
        (task 016 added its `ledgerRef?` field) REFERENCING the ledger entry `{bindingId}@t{n}` on the
        `compose`-disposition SSE frame — NEVER carrying the payload as source of truth.
    ADD ZERO new BFF routes and ZERO new PaneEventBus discriminants; NO string-key resolution outside the
    Binding table (ADR-039 §7.2). Add the §7.2 code-review checklist item.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript developer fluent in the SpaarkeAi three-pane PaneEventBus contract (ADR-030), the shipped Click-path session-dispatch seam, ADR-040 ledger-reference choreography, and Fluent v9 conventions.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A wired dispatch path where selecting text (or the doc-level overflow) in Compose dispatches any of the
    five catalog Bindings through the shipped Click-path seam with ZERO new routes and ZERO new PaneEventBus
    discriminants: the toolbar's `enqueueComposeAction` reaches `ConversationPane.dispatchComposeAction`
    (via `useSerialActionQueue` → `createConsumerDispatcher` → `dispatchConsumer(bindingId, {slots})`),
    streamed back as an assistant message; the existing `conversation.compose_selection_offer` choreography
    is consumed; and the draft-alternative apply leg emits the EXISTING `workspace.compose_assistant_insert`
    discriminant referencing the ledger entry `{bindingId}@t{n}` after the `compose`-disposition SSE frame.
    A code-review checklist item enforces §7.2 (no new endpoint, no string-key routing, NO new discriminant).
  </goal>

