  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + gate">Load task, project CLAUDE.md, compose-contracts.ts (the published discriminants), Spike 0 notes §4.1/§5, design §3 + §7.2. CONFIRM the shipped Click-path seam + the existing `compose_selection_offer`/`compose_assistant_insert` discriminants. The E-20/ComposeDisposition gate is SATISFIED — do NOT stop on it. (The invented-name divergence is already reconciled: this re-scoped POML IS the reconciliation.)</step>
    <step order="1" name="Verify/complete offer→dispatch hand-off">Trace ComposeAiToolbar `enqueueComposeAction` → `ConversationPane.dispatchComposeAction` (via useSerialActionQueue → createConsumerDispatcher → dispatchConsumer). If ComposeWorkspace does not already thread `dispatchComposeAction` into ComposeEditor, complete that wiring. Add ZERO new discriminants.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Confirm Flow 2 choreography">Confirm ComposeEditor emits the EXISTING `conversation.compose_selection_offer` (via useSelectionEventDispatch) and ConversationPane consumes it. Serial-queue (FR-18) honored.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Wire draft-alternative apply leg">On the `compose`-disposition SSE frame, emit the EXISTING `workspace.compose_assistant_insert` referencing the ledger entry (its `ledgerRef` = `{bindingId}@t{n}`, not the payload); the Workspace materializes the pending track-change (usePendingRedline) with that provenance.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Verify zero new routes + zero new discriminants">Route audit: confirm dispatch adds no new BFF route, no string-key resolution outside the Binding table, and NO new PaneEventBus discriminant. Add the §7.2 code-review checklist item. Add/adjust jest tests for the offer→dispatch hand-off + the compose_assistant_insert apply leg.</step>
  </steps>

