  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">Selecting text (or the doc-level overflow) and invoking a catalog action calls `enqueueComposeAction`, which reaches `ConversationPane.dispatchComposeAction` (useSerialActionQueue → createConsumerDispatcher → `dispatchConsumer(bindingId, {slots})`) — a DIRECT call, NOT a PaneEventBus event.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dispatch resolves through the shipped seam (POST /api/ai/chat/sessions/{id}/dispatch → SessionDispatchOrchestrator → GetBindingByIdAsync → executor) and adds ZERO new BFF routes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The compose-draft-alternative leg emits the EXISTING `workspace.compose_assistant_insert` discriminant REFERENCING the ledger entry (`ledgerRef`, never the payload) after the `compose`-disposition SSE frame.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ZERO new PaneEventBus discriminants are added — the ADR-030 closed union (compose_selection_offer + compose_assistant_insert) is untouched; `compose_action_request`/`compose_edit_apply_request` are NOT introduced. Client fetches use @spaarke/auth.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A route audit confirms no new BFF route, no string-key resolution outside the Binding table, and no new discriminant; the §7.2 code-review checklist item is present.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

