    <escalation-raised date="2026-07-09" resolved="true" resolution="Path C — POML re-scoped to compose-contracts.ts real flows; zero new discriminants">
      DIVERGENCE: this POML's goal + all 5 acceptance criteria + steps 1/3/4 are authored
      against two PaneEventBus discriminants — `compose_action_request` (conversation channel)
      and `compose_edit_apply_request` (workspace channel). Those names are RETRACTED
      "invented names" per four binding, code-grounded sources:
        1. Spike 0 (task 000) notes/spikes/spike-0-dispatch-path.md §4.1 + §5-crit-2:
           "`compose_action_request` does not exist and must not be created … Impacted
           tasks: 030, 016, 046 (dispatch wiring — wire the offer→dispatch path, NOT an
           `compose_action_request` handler)." Spike 0 names THIS task explicitly.
        2. design.md §7.2 (line 465), the POML's own cited authority: "(Spike 0 correction,
           2026-07-08: there is no `compose_action_request` / `compose_edit_apply_request`
           event in the code; those were invented names. The real contract is
           compose-contracts.ts.)"
        3. ComposeEditor.tsx file JSDoc (lines 40-45): "NOT a `compose_action_request`
           PaneEventBus event (never existed; do not add one)."
        4. useSerialActionQueue.ts JSDoc (Contract-naming note): the discriminant name was
           retracted; the toolbar calls dispatchConsumer DIRECTLY; "no PaneEventBus
           discriminant is introduced or required (ADR-030's closed union is untouched)."

      REAL (published) contract per compose-contracts.ts:
        - Dispatch TRIGGER = direct `dispatchConsumer(bindingId, {slots})` (the shipped
          Click-path seam), NOT a bus event. Already wired: ComposeEditor mounts
          ComposeAiToolbar (task 030) with `enqueueComposeAction`; ConversationPane exposes
          `dispatchComposeAction` via useSerialActionQueue → createConsumerDispatcher.
        - Flow 2 = `conversation.compose_selection_offer` (EXISTING; ComposeEditor already
          emits it via useSelectionEventDispatch) — pane choreography, not the trigger.
        - Flow 5 apply leg = `workspace.compose_assistant_insert` (EXISTING; task 016 added
          its `ledgerRef?` field) REFERENCING the ledger entry after the compose SSE frame —
          this is the POML's "compose_edit_apply_request" leg under its real name.

      Following the POML literally would: (a) add two dead discriminants to the ADR-030
      closed union that design.md says must stay untouched; (b) re-introduce a parallel
      dispatch-trigger mechanism Spike 0 + ADR-039 forbid; (c) directly violate ComposeEditor's
      own "do not add one" binding comment. It would also duplicate already-shipped wiring
      (016/030/032).

      RECOMMENDED RESOLUTION: Path C (pivot to comply — CLAUDE.md §6.5). Re-scope 046 to:
        (i) verify/complete the offer→dispatch hand-off (ComposeWorkspace threading
            ConversationPane.dispatchComposeAction → ComposeEditor.enqueueComposeAction);
        (ii) emit `workspace.compose_assistant_insert` (Flow 5) referencing the ledger
            entry (ledgerRef `{bindingId}@t{n}`) on the compose-disposition SSE frame;
        (iii) add the §7.2 code-review checklist item (zero new routes / no string-key
            routing / NO new PaneEventBus discriminant).
      Add ZERO new PaneEventBus discriminants. Requires human/parent confirmation of the
      re-scope + updated acceptance criteria before implementation resumes (a silent pivot
      would itself violate the "do not adapt silently" instruction).
    </escalation-raised>
